{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Figure 4 shows histogram of spectral reach of toy model implementing maps P_SK, P_lite, P_krom, P_go on random targets in B_4.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "P_SK",
        "P_lite",
        "P_krom",
        "P_go",
        "B_4"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Blue and green lines in (a-e) are boundaries of spectra of B_3\\B_2 and B_4\\B_3 polytopes.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "B_3",
        "B_2",
        "B_4"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "(a) mHC contains points outside B_4.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "mHC",
        "B_4"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "(b) mHC-lite fills region near boundary almost completely without extending past it.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "mHC-lite"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "(c) KromHC fails to represent complex region inside B_4 because its shadow is 1-dimensional, filling infinitesimal slice.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "KromHC",
        "B_4"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "(d) For s=1, go-mHC represents sizeable portion of region but cannot represent all matrices near boundary of polytope.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "s=1",
        "go-mHC",
        "polytope"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "(e) With s=2, go-mHC begins to represent larger regions of B_4, filling region more densely.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000078"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "s=2",
        "go-mHC",
        "B_4"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Figure illustrates Karpelevič region for dimensions d=2 to d=5.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000079"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Karpelevič region",
        "d"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "If a method's spectrum is clustered in a small sub-region, it is poorly expressive; filling Karpelevič region captures diverse dynamics.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000079"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Karpelevič region"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Spectral reach of mHC, KromHC, and go-mHC shown in figures 3 and 4.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000079"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "mHC",
        "KromHC",
        "go-mHC",
        "figures 3",
        "4"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "4.1.1 Eigenvalue Coverage of s-ssostochastic Matrices",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000080"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "Eigenvalue Coverage of s-ssostochastic Matrices"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Eigenvalue distribution of s-ssostochastic matrices is constrained by membership in Birkhoff polytope B_d and residence within Karpelevič region.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000081"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "s-ssostochastic matrices",
        "Birkhoff polytope",
        "B_d",
        "Karpelevič region"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "11-orthostochastic matrices have restricted hypo-cycloidal boundary; increasing parameter s provides denser approximation of B_d.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000081"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "11-orthostochastic matrices",
        "s",
        "B_d"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "As s increases, spectral support of ss-orthostochastic matrices expands to fill Karpelevič region, approaching density of general doubly stochastic matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000081"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "s",
        "ss-orthostochastic matrices",
        "Karpelevič region",
        "doubly stochastic matrices"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "4.1.2 The Spectral Limitation of Kronecker Products",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000082"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "The Spectral Limitation of Kronecker Products"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "KromHC imposes symmetry on d-streams that prunes mixing terms in H_res.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000083"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "KromHC",
        "d-streams",
        "H_res"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "KromHC parameterizes only a sparse subset of B_d for d>2 by analyzing spectral reach of k-fold Kronecker products.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000083"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "KromHC",
        "B_d",
        "d>2",
        "k-fold Kronecker products"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Spectral space of k-fold Kronecker product of doubly stochastic matrices is invariant to index k, restricting expressive reach to base manifold.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000083"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "k-fold Kronecker product",
        "doubly stochastic matrices",
        "index k"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Formal proof of this invariance is in Appendix B.3.1.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000083"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Appendix B.3.1"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Example 4×4 case: matrices A,B ∈ B_2 have spectra {1,λ_A} and {1,λ_B} with λ∈[-1,1].",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000084"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "A",
        "B",
        "B_2",
        "λ",
        "[-1,1]"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Spectrum of Kronecker product A⊗B is {1,λ_A,λ_B,λ_A λ_B} which remains within [-1,1] and inside spectral hull of B_2.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000084"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "A⊗B",
        "λ_A",
        "λ_B",
        "B_2"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Therefore spectral reach of Kronecker-parameterized manifold is invariant to number of products and fails to expand into broader Karpelevič region, representing negligible portion of B_d when d>i_k.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000084"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Kronecker-parameterized manifold",
        "Karpelevič region",
        "B_d",
        "d>i_k"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Empirically shows O(d) additional error in minimum achievable loss compared to mHC-lite and go-mHC.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000084"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "O(d) error",
        "mHC-lite",
        "go-mHC"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Collapse in spectral volume for Kronecker-based transforms causes loss of functional diversity.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000085"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Kronecker-based transforms"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Constraints fail to represent cyclic permutations of order greater than i_k=2 (e.g., 1→2→3→1), preventing learning complex periodic dependencies.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000085"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "cyclic permutations",
        "i_k=2",
        "1→2→3→1"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Restriction to real eigenvalues in 2×2 base case implies only pure diffusion without advection, limiting directional flow of signals.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000085"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "real eigenvalues",
        "2×2",
        "pure diffusion",
        "advection",
        "directional flow"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
